# Game Debug UI & Runtime Profiler Tools

This skill defines architecture and conventions for embedding high-speed developer tooling, immediate-mode overlays, live parameter tuning, and CPU/GPU timeline profiling inside game engines.

---

## 1. Dear ImGui Integration Architecture

* **Backend Render Hooks:**
  Hook into the existing engine render graph as a post-tonemap pass writing directly to the backbuffer before presentation.
* **Input Interception Protocol:**
  * When `ImGui::GetIO().WantCaptureMouse` is true, suppress mouse clicks from passing down to gameplay camera/action systems.
  * When `ImGui::GetIO().WantCaptureKeyboard` is true, suppress keystrokes from character controllers.
  * Always allow toggling the debug console hotkey (e.g. `~` / `F1`) unconditionally.

---

## 2. Immediate-Mode 3D Debug Renderer (`DebugDraw`)

Gameplay and physics code should draw debug geometry in a single line without managing lifetime objects:
```cpp
class DebugDraw {
public:
    static void Line(const Vec3& start, const Vec3& end, Color color, float duration = 0.0f);
    static void Box(const Vec3& center, const Vec3& extents, Color color, float duration = 0.0f);
    static void Sphere(const Vec3& center, float radius, Color color, float duration = 0.0f);
    static void Frustum(const Mat4& invViewProj, Color color, float duration = 0.0f);
    static void Normal(const Vec3& pos, const Vec3& normal, float length = 0.5f);
};
```
* **Ring Buffer Allocation:** Pre-allocate a 2MB dynamic vertex buffer (`struct DebugVertex { float pos[3]; uint32_t color; }`). Accumulate lines every frame, issue a single `DrawIndexed` call, and reset the pointer on VSYNC.

